('1900a542-a9e9-560a-8148-c65cd14a276f'::uuid, 'Anatomy Histology Embryology (Paper 1)', 'Special Histology - Special Senses', 'Which option best describes the three chambers of the eye?', '["Only anterior and posterior","Anterior chamber (between cornea and iris)","posterior chamber (between iris and lens)","and vitreous chamber (behind lens)","Only vitreous chamber"]'::jsonb, 'Anterior chamber (between cornea and iris)', 'The eye contains three chambers: the anterior chamber between cornea and iris, the posterior chamber between iris and lens, and the vitreous chamber behind the lens. Options that list only two compartments or only the vitreous chamber omit parts of the three-chamber arrangement.'),
