('87caf0db-89c0-5f25-8c4a-3d541184e3dd'::uuid, 'Anatomy Histology Embryology (Paper 1)', 'Special Histology - Special Senses', 'Which option best describes the five layers of the cornea (anterior to posterior)?', '["Corneal epithelium","stroma (substantia propria)","Bowman''s layer","and corneal endothelium","Descemet''s membrane"]'::jsonb, 'Corneal epithelium', 'The corneal layers in anteroposterior order are epithelium, Bowman''s layer, stroma (substantia propria), Descemet''s membrane, and endothelium. The epithelium is the surface layer, so it heads the proper sequence.'),
