('32defb0b-7685-59ba-859a-7be3b8862090'::uuid, 'Physiology (Paper 2)', 'Respiratory System - Respiratory Part 2', 'A 22-year-old school teacher develops sudden breathlessness and tachycardia post-surgery. V/Q scan shows a ventilation-perfusion mismatch with normal ventilation but no perfusion. (Respiratory Case #74)', '["Anatomic shunt only resulting in decreased functional activity","Hypoventilation accompanied by associated clinical symptoms","Diffusion limitation mediated by specific receptor activation","Alveolar dead space only without affecting the primary tissue pathway","Ventilation-perfusion (V/Q) mismatch and shunt"]'::jsonb, 'Ventilation-perfusion (V/Q) mismatch and shunt', 'A pulmonary embolism causes V/Q mismatch and shunt, leading to hypoxemia.'),
('7844fa6e-b6a3-5d9e-a267-d0a7347954c1'::uuid, 'Physiology (Paper 2)', 'Respiratory System - Respiratory Part 2', 'A 61-year-old office clerk presents with chest tightness and cough that worsens at night. PFTs show an obstructive pattern that is reversible with a bronchodilator. (Respiratory Case #75)', '["Emphysema","Sarcoidosis","Chronic bronchitis","Idiopathic pulmonary fibrosis","Asthma"]'::jsonb, 'Asthma', 'Asthma is characterized by a reversible obstructive airway pattern, showing >12% improvement in FEV1 post-bronchodilator.'),
