('a6f2b18d-c5d3-5216-88d0-c13cb92b95b1'::uuid, 'Physiology (Paper 2)', 'Respiratory System - Respiratory Part 2', 'A 52-year-old female presents with sudden-onset pleuritic chest pain and dyspnea after a long-distance flight. ABG shows hypoxemia, hypocapnia, and a respiratory alkalosis. (Respiratory Case #78)', '["Hypoventilation resulting in decreased functional activity","Ventilation-perfusion (V/Q) mismatch and shunt","Diffusion limitation mediated by specific receptor activation","Anatomic shunt only without affecting the primary tissue pathway","Alveolar dead space only leading to subsequent cellular adaptation"]'::jsonb, 'Ventilation-perfusion (V/Q) mismatch and shunt', 'A pulmonary embolism causes V/Q mismatch and shunt, leading to hypoxemia.'),
