('d0932c42-57af-5d5c-a61e-07d1b4849143'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 1)', 'General Pharmacology - General Pharmacology', 'Receptor upregulation occurs with:', '["Chronic agonist use resulting in decreased functional activity","Chronic antagonist use (denervation supersensitivity)","Single dose of agonist mediated by specific receptor activation","Acute exposure without affecting the primary tissue pathway","Short-term treatment leading to subsequent cellular adaptation"]'::jsonb, 'Chronic antagonist use (denervation supersensitivity)', 'Chronic blockade increases receptor number/sensitivity.'),
('9a9ab2b8-1483-5229-a919-dbd7347f690c'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 1)', 'General Pharmacology - General Pharmacology', 'Regarding clinical cases in General Pharmacology: Acetaminophen toxic metabolite:', '["NAPQI","MPP+","MPTP","N-oxide","Sulfate conjugate"]'::jsonb, 'NAPQI', 'NAPQI normally detoxified by glutathione. Overdose depletes glutathione.'),
('537f3da5-23f4-540f-bbe7-432d8690283b'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 1)', 'General Pharmacology - General Pharmacology', 'In the study of General Pharmacology, Acetaminophen antidote:', '["N-acetylcysteine","Flumazenil","Naloxone","Fomepizole","Deferoxamine"]'::jsonb, 'N-acetylcysteine', 'NAC replenishes glutathione stores.'),
('d53a59ec-9268-54e2-ba11-93ae61d2028d'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 1)', 'General Pharmacology - General Pharmacology', 'ED50 is the dose that produces:', '["Toxicity in 50% resulting in decreased functional activity","Desired effect in 50% of population","Death in 50% mediated by specific receptor activation","Maximum effect without affecting the primary tissue pathway","No effect leading to subsequent cellular adaptation"]'::jsonb, 'Desired effect in 50% of population', 'ED50 = median effective dose.'),
('812c5808-6795-50a3-b558-5a48f58200cc'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 1)', 'General Pharmacology - General Pharmacology', 'TD50 is the dose that produces:', '["Therapeutic effect in 50%","Toxic effect in 50% of population","Death in 50%","No effect in 50%","Maximum effect"]'::jsonb, 'Toxic effect in 50% of population', 'TD50 = median toxic dose.'),
('5bc7f162-8f15-5a70-b583-7b1a24ecb7e5'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 1)', 'General Pharmacology - General Pharmacology', 'High therapeutic index means drug is:', '["More dangerous","Safer","Less effective","More potent","Has narrow window"]'::jsonb, 'Safer', 'High TI = large gap between therapeutic and toxic doses.'),
