('cb6a9343-781c-584d-ae26-90dc4d468715'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 1)', 'Autonomic Nervous System - ANS Pharmacology', 'Which of the following features constitutes the anticholinergic toxidrome?', '["Miosis, salivation, diarrhea","Mydriasis, dry mouth, tachycardia, hot dry skin","Bradycardia, sweating, miosis","Hypotension, miosis, bronchorrhea","Nystagmus, salivation, bradycardia"]'::jsonb, 'Mydriasis, dry mouth, tachycardia, hot dry skin', 'Anticholinergic toxidrome: mydriasis, dry mouth, tachycardia, hot dry skin, urinary retention.'),
