('1ef5fcd5-bf7f-5f77-83d1-d74e6fc654ec'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 1)', 'Autonomic Nervous System - ANS Pharmacology', 'Atropine is given as a preanesthetic medication to:', '["Increases secretions","Decreases respiratory and salivary secretions","Induces anesthesia","Provides analgesia","Causes muscle relaxation"]'::jsonb, 'Decreases respiratory and salivary secretions', 'Atropine reduces secretions to prevent aspiration.'),
('4b7e0f0a-cbbd-5280-9c09-d35d911686cc'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 1)', 'Autonomic Nervous System - ANS Pharmacology', 'Ipratropium is best administered by inhalation because this route provides:', '["Better oral absorption resulting in decreased functional activity","Local bronchodilation with minimal systemic effects","Cannot be given IV mediated by specific receptor activation","Cheaper by this route without affecting the primary tissue pathway","Shorter half-life IV leading to subsequent cellular adaptation"]'::jsonb, 'Local bronchodilation with minimal systemic effects', 'Inhaled ipratropium provides local effect with reduced systemic side effects.'),
