('b3f0698d-606d-57e8-8acb-cd048eba9ad5'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 1)', 'Autonomic Nervous System - ANS Pharmacology', 'Ingestion of tyramine-rich food by a patient taking a MAO inhibitor causes:', '["Excessive ACh accumulation resulting in decreased functional activity","Excessive tyramine causing hypertensive crisis","Serotonin syndrome mediated by specific receptor activation","Hypoglycemia without affecting the primary tissue pathway","Bradycardia leading to subsequent cellular adaptation"]'::jsonb, 'Excessive tyramine causing hypertensive crisis', 'MAO inhibitors prevent tyramine metabolism, causing massive NE release.'),
