('48c5e7c5-a875-5508-8e32-4e5877bbe59a'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'ISTH recommends which DOAC for CrCl 15-30:', '["Dabigatran","Rivaroxaban","Apixaban","Edoxaban","All equal"]'::jsonb, 'Apixaban', 'Apixaban: most favorable safety data in severe renal impairment.'),
('cb957e94-0790-5fb5-b4ac-a78f56415897'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'IV iron indicated when:', '["Mild iron deficiency resulting in decreased functional activity","Oral iron not tolerated/malabsorption","Hb 14 g/dL mediated by specific receptor activation","Pregnant at term without affecting the primary tissue pathway","Ferritin 500 leading to subsequent cellular adaptation"]'::jsonb, 'Oral iron not tolerated/malabsorption', 'IV iron for oral intolerance, malabsorption, CKD on EPO, rapid repletion.'),
('4d9efb7e-8076-57ec-a1c4-7ec64d9aadc5'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'IWPC algorithm integrates:', '["VKORC1+CYP2C9+clinical factors","Only clinical","Only genetic","Dietary only","Age only"]'::jsonb, 'VKORC1+CYP2C9+clinical factors', 'Integrates genotypes with age, weight, medications, etc.'),
('60f82ac9-7849-56bf-93d8-7de780297171'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'Immunothrombosis refers interplay between:', '["Innate immunity and coagulation (neutrophils, platelets, complement, NETs)","Only platelets accompanied by associated clinical symptoms","Only coagulation factors mediated by specific receptor activation","RBCs only without affecting the primary tissue pathway","Lymphocytes only leading to subsequent cellular adaptation"]'::jsonb, 'Innate immunity and coagulation (neutrophils, platelets, complement, NETs)', 'Interplay of innate immunity and coagulation in host defense and thrombosis.'),
('71b150c6-81ae-5b5b-bf47-337187c958e9'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'Individualized antiplatelet therapy considers:', '["Only age resulting in decreased functional activity","Genetic polymorphisms (CYP2C19, GPIIIa), clinical factors, platelet function testing","Only weight mediated by specific receptor activation","Only gender without affecting the primary tissue pathway","Only renal function leading to subsequent cellular adaptation"]'::jsonb, 'Genetic polymorphisms (CYP2C19, GPIIIa), clinical factors, platelet function testing', 'Integrates genetics, clinical factors, and platelet function for optimal selection/dosing.'),
('8f187c26-131e-58bf-8fce-bbed96b6da57'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'Iron absorption enhanced by:', '["Calcium","Tannins","Vitamin C","Antacids","Phytates"]'::jsonb, 'Vitamin C', 'Vitamin C reduces Fe3+ to Fe2+, the absorbable form.'),
('5741574f-5c64-51e2-9457-bcc37466df77'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'LMWH differs from UFH by:', '["Greater anti-IIa activity","Greater anti-Xa:anti-IIa ratio","Requires routine aPTT","Shorter half-life","Greater protein binding"]'::jsonb, 'Greater anti-Xa:anti-IIa ratio', 'LMWH: anti-Xa:anti-IIa ratio 2:1-4:1 vs UFH 1:1.'),
('fc06678e-4f0e-5de2-9c26-0b636c63240c'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'LMWH needs no routine monitoring because:', '["No effect resulting in decreased functional activity","More predictable pharmacokinetics","SC route mediated by specific receptor activation","Not absorbed without affecting the primary tissue pathway","No side effects leading to subsequent cellular adaptation"]'::jsonb, 'More predictable pharmacokinetics', 'Predictable dose-response allows fixed dosing.'),
('8f9a119b-7d21-5da4-9932-2597c3b3f4ce'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'Leucovorin rescue works because:', '["Antagonizes MTX directly","Provides reduced folate bypassing DHFR block","Increases MTX excretion","Binds MTX in plasma","Stimulates MTX metabolism"]'::jsonb, 'Provides reduced folate bypassing DHFR block', 'Leucovorin provides reduced folate downstream of DHFR block.'),
('17d9104a-aecd-5dbd-89ec-1a239e7bd0fe'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'Life-threatening warfarin bleeding antidote:', '["Protamine","4-factor PCC + IV vitamin K","TXA","Desmopressin","Platelet transfusion"]'::jsonb, '4-factor PCC + IV vitamin K', 'PCC provides immediate factors + IV vitamin K for sustained reversal.'),
('edacd23c-e854-5113-b898-c4b76119cfe2'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'Longest half-life VK-dependent factor:', '["Factor VII","Factor IX","Factor X","Factor II (prothrombin)","Protein C"]'::jsonb, 'Factor II (prothrombin)', 'Factor II 60-72h; explains warfarin full effect delay.'),
('509291ba-204e-5184-974e-cf67fe287e92'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'Major antifibrinolytic adverse effect:', '["Hypoglycemia resulting in decreased functional activity","Thromboembolic complications (DVT, PE, stroke)","Hypotension mediated by specific receptor activation","Renal failure without affecting the primary tissue pathway","Alopecia leading to subsequent cellular adaptation"]'::jsonb, 'Thromboembolic complications (DVT, PE, stroke)', 'Inhibit clot breakdown, predisposing to thromboembolism.'),
('5c3d76b3-51b2-55f6-855e-d0c9bf07c65f'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'Major complication of all thrombolytics:', '["Hypertension","Bleeding (including ICH)","Thrombosis","Hypoglycemia","Arrhythmia"]'::jsonb, 'Bleeding (including ICH)', 'ICH occurs 0.5-1% of patients; most feared complication.'),
('e1f7d94e-187d-51cf-b755-dd13ede16f2f'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'Major concern repeated factor VIII infusions:', '["Hypertension resulting in decreased functional activity","Inhibitors (neutralizing alloantibodies)","Diabetes mediated by specific receptor activation","Renal failure without affecting the primary tissue pathway","Osteoporosis leading to subsequent cellular adaptation"]'::jsonb, 'Inhibitors (neutralizing alloantibodies)', '25-30% severe hemophilia A develop inhibitors against exogenous VIII.'),
('ecb489d4-e359-54cd-b6d0-d8b6ca660a14'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'Mechanical aortic valve target INR:', '["1.5-2.0","2.0-3.0","2.5-3.5","3.0-4.0","4.0-5.0"]'::jsonb, '2.0-3.0', 'Mechanical aortic valve (no other risk factors): 2.0-3.0.'),
('938ffb6b-4a25-536f-b13d-fa2c13be96d7'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'Mechanical mitral valve INR 1.8 should:', '["Increase warfarin (target 2.5-3.5)","Decrease dose accompanied by associated clinical symptoms","Stop warfarin mediated by specific receptor activation","Switch to aspirin without affecting the primary tissue pathway","Start DOAC leading to subsequent cellular adaptation"]'::jsonb, 'Increase warfarin (target 2.5-3.5)', 'Mitral valve target 2.5-3.5; INR 1.8 subtherapeutic.'),
('c35cb368-fba2-525f-a8ce-6e903cbc18d2'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'Megaloblastic anemia characteristic finding:', '["Microcytic RBCs resulting in decreased functional activity","Macrocytosis with hypersegmented neutrophils","Spherocytes mediated by specific receptor activation","Target cells without affecting the primary tissue pathway","Schistocytes leading to subsequent cellular adaptation"]'::jsonb, 'Macrocytosis with hypersegmented neutrophils', 'MCV >100 fL with hypersegmented neutrophils (>=5 lobes).'),
('1a43c545-f5e8-5cc8-bb21-34663c2ab91d'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'Methotrexate causes folate deficiency by:', '["Blocking absorption","Inhibiting dihydrofolate reductase (DHFR)","Increasing renal excretion","Destroying liver stores","Inhibiting transport"]'::jsonb, 'Inhibiting dihydrofolate reductase (DHFR)', 'Inhibits DHFR, preventing conversion to active tetrahydrofolate.'),
('77b0cd9f-5fbe-537a-8cad-9c6a42f92629'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'Methotrexate toxicity antidote:', '["Vitamin K resulting in decreased functional activity","Leucovorin (folinic acid)","Protamine mediated by specific receptor activation","Desmopressin without affecting the primary tissue pathway","TXA leading to subsequent cellular adaptation"]'::jsonb, 'Leucovorin (folinic acid)', 'Leucovorin provides reduced folate bypassing DHFR block.'),
('5e848ce7-bd9f-578d-89e1-717787971bf4'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'Methylmalonic acid elevated in deficiency of:', '["Folate","Iron","Vitamin B12","Vitamin C","Vitamin D"]'::jsonb, 'Vitamin B12', 'Methylmalonyl-CoA mutase requires B12; elevated MMA specific for B12 deficiency.'),
('d5e2d47b-3c8d-5d44-9190-3cfcc010c255'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'Most clinically significant warfarin interaction:', '["Aspirin increasing INR","Rifampin decreasing INR via CYP induction","Paracetamol no effect","Ibuprofen no effect","All minor"]'::jsonb, 'Rifampin decreasing INR via CYP induction', 'Rifampin: most significant CYP inducer, >50% warfarin effect reduction.'),
('94eba1fd-2e48-5173-ac11-60e55c34a2f2'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'Most common B12 deficiency cause?', '["Dietary","Pernicious anemia","Crohn''s","Fish tapeworm","Medications"]'::jsonb, 'Pernicious anemia', 'Pernicious anemia (autoimmune gastritis, loss of intrinsic factor) is most common.'),
('7b0478df-36c6-5fd9-a5e9-75dcdee088c6'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'Most common EPO side effect:', '["Hepatotoxicity","Hypertension","Hypoglycemia","Alopecia","Pancreatitis"]'::jsonb, 'Hypertension', 'Hypertension in 20-30% from increased viscosity and vascular effects.'),
('80ed738e-13e1-563e-97ff-6c56edc8fd92'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'Most common G-CSF side effect:', '["Nephrotoxicity","Bone pain at injection site","Hepatotoxicity","Ototoxicity","Pulmonary fibrosis"]'::jsonb, 'Bone pain at injection site', 'Bone pain from marrow expansion in up to 30% of patients.'),
('59bf0ac5-df91-5f8d-800c-ace4989a4571'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'Most common HIT thrombotic complication:', '["Arterial","DVT","Intracranial hemorrhage","Pulmonary hemorrhage","GI hemorrhage"]'::jsonb, 'DVT', 'Venous thrombosis (DVT/PE) more common than arterial.'),
('687179ee-bfe2-5323-a342-5cf26fb268bf'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'Most common inherited thrombophilia:', '["AT III deficiency","Protein C deficiency","Factor V Leiden (APC resistance)","Prothrombin G20210A","Antiphospholipid syndrome"]'::jsonb, 'Factor V Leiden (APC resistance)', 'Factor V Leiden found in 5% Caucasians; most common inherited thrombophilia.'),
('4a92faaa-1a78-5a2b-ba7f-b220181120cd'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'Most common oral iron supplement?', '["Ferric pyrophosphate","Ferrous sulfate","Ferrous gluconate","Ferrous fumarate","Iron dextran"]'::jsonb, 'Ferrous sulfate', 'Ferrous sulfate is most common, least expensive, most widely available.'),
('fdbccb41-dbc5-5970-9a9c-02e700135b2a'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'Most common side effect of oral iron?', '["Hepatotoxicity resulting in decreased functional activity","Constipation, nausea, epigastric discomfort","Aplastic anemia mediated by specific receptor activation","Hyperkalemia without affecting the primary tissue pathway","Pancreatitis leading to subsequent cellular adaptation"]'::jsonb, 'Constipation, nausea, epigastric discomfort', 'GI side effects affect up to 60% of patients on oral iron.'),
('13dc8949-1fe3-5832-ad2f-9cffeee099b2'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'Most dangerous thrombolytic complication:', '["Hypotension","Intracranial hemorrhage","Arrhythmia","Nausea","Allergic reaction"]'::jsonb, 'Intracranial hemorrhage', 'ICH 0.5-1%; most feared complication.'),
('0a371c36-2927-5550-9763-d473db1368fe'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'Most serious deferasirox effect:', '["Constipation resulting in decreased functional activity","Renal failure accompanied by associated clinical symptoms","GI hemorrhage and renal/hepatic failure","Dizziness without affecting the primary tissue pathway","Weight gain leading to subsequent cellular adaptation"]'::jsonb, 'GI hemorrhage and renal/hepatic failure', 'Serious: GI hemorrhage, renal/hepatic failure, bone marrow suppression.'),
('6551d8e3-c8c0-556d-b768-789be6deac93'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'Most specific marker for recent thrombin generation:', '["Fibrinogen resulting in decreased functional activity","D-dimer accompanied by associated clinical symptoms","Prothrombin fragment 1+2 (F1+2)","Platelet count without affecting the primary tissue pathway","aPTT leading to subsequent cellular adaptation"]'::jsonb, 'Prothrombin fragment 1+2 (F1+2)', 'F1+2 released when prothrombin converted to thrombin; directly reflects generation.'),
('87ac05df-1112-5677-ad0a-82991e68d7ec'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'NOT a cause of macrocytosis:', '["Alcoholism","Hypothyroidism","Iron deficiency anemia","Reticulocytosis","Liver disease"]'::jsonb, 'Iron deficiency anemia', 'Iron deficiency causes microcytosis, not macrocytosis.'),
('5cab9c63-cceb-55a3-a0c8-4ce87d97e1a6'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'Neural tube defects prevented by:', '["Vitamin B12","Iron","Folic acid","Vitamin D","Calcium"]'::jsonb, 'Folic acid', 'Periconceptional folic acid (400-800 mcg/day) reduces NTD risk 70%.'),
('f94d4213-7ba4-5b75-b6ea-b45ed0d6b79a'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'Neurological symptoms in deficiency of:', '["Iron","Vitamin B12","Vitamin C","Vitamin D","Folic acid"]'::jsonb, 'Vitamin B12', 'Neurological manifestations characteristic of B12 deficiency; absent in folate deficiency.'),
('4b74ae7b-8a7a-5d84-9bd3-04897ab3e3c8'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'On-treatment platelet reactivity assessed to:', '["Adherence only resulting in decreased functional activity","Predict thrombotic/bleeding risk and response to therapy","Liver function mediated by specific receptor activation","Kidney function without affecting the primary tissue pathway","Hematocrit leading to subsequent cellular adaptation"]'::jsonb, 'Predict thrombotic/bleeding risk and response to therapy', 'High reactivity = thrombotic risk; low = bleeding risk.'),
('c26e8bbd-50bb-54ce-9072-e2eb29f015b7'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'Oral iron chelators include:', '["Deferoxamine","Deferasirox","Deferiprone","D-Penicillamine","Both deferasirox and deferiprone"]'::jsonb, 'Both deferasirox and deferiprone', 'Both deferasirox and deferiprone are oral; deferoxamine is parenteral only.'),
('3baad566-a933-58f0-8249-e3d197a24940'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'P2Y12 inhibitor with fastest offset for surgery planning:', '["Clopidogrel","Ticagrelor (reversibility)","Prasugrel","All equal","Aspirin"]'::jsonb, 'Ticagrelor (reversibility)', 'Reversibility allows faster function recovery (3-5 days) vs irreversible agents.'),
('0a528440-1e75-5980-b307-564eb459e620'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'PF4-heparin complex forms because:', '["Heparin binds AT III resulting in decreased functional activity","Heparin binds PF4 (alpha granules), creating neoantigen","PF4 produced by heparin mediated by specific receptor activation","Heparin inhibits PF4 without affecting the primary tissue pathway","PF4 destroys heparin leading to subsequent cellular adaptation"]'::jsonb, 'Heparin binds PF4 (alpha granules), creating neoantigen', 'Heparin-PF4 binding creates neoantigen recognized by immune system.'),
('8153f2cf-9100-5fc2-9e90-bccf2e19fd52'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'PLATO trial interaction with:', '["Warfarin resulting in decreased functional activity","Aspirin (high-dose may reduce ticagrelor efficacy)","Statins mediated by specific receptor activation","Beta-blockers without affecting the primary tissue pathway","ACE inhibitors leading to subsequent cellular adaptation"]'::jsonb, 'Aspirin (high-dose may reduce ticagrelor efficacy)', 'High-dose aspirin (>300mg) may reduce ticagrelor benefit vs clopidogrel.'),
('5a30b02d-e0ee-5e6e-9b1b-4b68e85c6a1b'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'PLATO trial ticagrelor vs clopidogrel showed:', '["No difference resulting in decreased functional activity","Significant reduction in CV death, MI, or stroke","Increased bleeding only mediated by specific receptor activation","Increased mortality without affecting the primary tissue pathway","No benefit leading to subsequent cellular adaptation"]'::jsonb, 'Significant reduction in CV death, MI, or stroke', 'Ticagrelor superior to clopidogrel in ACS.'),
('4a6fc7f9-3d3e-51fe-9521-07a24155c684'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'POC testing for antiplatelet therapy includes:', '["Standard CBC","VerifyNow (Accumetrics)","Standard coagulation analyzer","Blood gas analyzer","Electrolyte analyzer"]'::jsonb, 'VerifyNow (Accumetrics)', 'VerifyNow: POC device measuring aspirin, P2Y12, and GPIIb/IIIa response.'),
('b9c29009-eebe-5506-af83-948cc2a1e915'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'PRU measured by VerifyNow assesses:', '["Aspirin response","P2Y12 inhibitor response","GPIIb/IIIa inhibition","Platelet count","Hemoglobin"]'::jsonb, 'P2Y12 inhibitor response', 'Lower PRU = greater P2Y12 inhibition; predicts antiplatelet response.'),
('f3a9f4e0-fdcc-5a39-8bbc-238178a76d4a'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'PT/INR measures:', '["Intrinsic pathway","Extrinsic pathway (factor VII dependent)","Common pathway only","Platelet function","Fibrinolytic pathway"]'::jsonb, 'Extrinsic pathway (factor VII dependent)', 'Most sensitive to factor VII (extrinsic pathway).'),
('452eaac7-8ece-58fe-b2ba-a73060c842a2'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'Pegfilgrastim preferred over filgrastim because:', '["More potent resulting in decreased functional activity","Longer half-life, once-per-cycle dosing","No side effects mediated by specific receptor activation","Oral route without affecting the primary tissue pathway","Cheaper leading to subsequent cellular adaptation"]'::jsonb, 'Longer half-life, once-per-cycle dosing', 'PEGylation extends half-life allowing once-per-cycle dosing.'),
('eac1a847-cabd-5253-a9f5-f5413cfba9b8'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'Perioperative warfarin stopped 5 days before because:', '["Takes 5 days elimination resulting in decreased functional activity","Takes 5 days for most procoagulant factors (especially II) to clear","It is stored in fat mediated by specific receptor activation","Rapid metabolism without affecting the primary tissue pathway","It is not absorbed leading to subsequent cellular adaptation"]'::jsonb, 'Takes 5 days for most procoagulant factors (especially II) to clear', 'Factor II t1/2 60-72h; 5 days needed for therapeutic levels to clear.'),
('7409cda8-6d1b-5183-adc2-211b5f92419c'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'Pharmacogenomic warfarin dosing recommended by:', '["WHO only","FDA, CPIC, DPWG","FDA only","No guidelines","ESC only"]'::jsonb, 'FDA, CPIC, DPWG', 'All major guidelines recommend incorporating VKORC1 and CYP2C9.'),
('0a6104f5-5cab-53a9-918b-4cb8ab61c450'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'Pharmacogenomic warfarin dosing validated by:', '["RE-LY","EU-PACT","TRITON-TIMI 38","CRASH-2","PLATO"]'::jsonb, 'EU-PACT', 'EU-PACT and COAG trials validated genotyping approaches.'),
('8a42baf5-2b14-541c-9c02-003ee82d4831'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'Pharmacokinetic variability particularly important for:', '["DOACs resulting in decreased functional activity","Warfarin (genetic, drug, food interactions)","Heparin (no variability) mediated by specific receptor activation","LMWH (no variability) without affecting the primary tissue pathway","Aspirin (no variability leading to subsequent cellular adaptation"]'::jsonb, 'Warfarin (genetic, drug, food interactions)', 'Marked variability from genetics (VKORC1, CYP2C9), drugs, diet, disease state.'),
('0b0a56f2-8072-5a2c-ba0b-fbde7b23c56f'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'Phenytoin causes megaloblastic anemia via:', '["Iron absorption","B12 absorption","Folic acid metabolism","Vitamin K","Vitamin D"]'::jsonb, 'Folic acid metabolism', 'Phenytoin interferes with folate absorption/metabolism.'),
('c4f2b714-5215-56a5-8394-30790f7dc43b'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'Platelet reactivity index (PRI) measures:', '["Aspirin response resulting in decreased functional activity","P2Y12 inhibitor response (VASP phosphorylation assay)","GPIIb/IIIa function mediated by specific receptor activation","Platelet count without affecting the primary tissue pathway","Bleeding time leading to subsequent cellular adaptation"]'::jsonb, 'P2Y12 inhibitor response (VASP phosphorylation assay)', 'VASP phosphorylation: specifically measures P2Y12 inhibition.'),
('bb1ad1d1-cc25-51aa-b927-acbf204b24d1'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'Population with HIGHEST warfarin dose requirements:', '["East Asians","Caucasians","African Americans","South Asians","All equal"]'::jsonb, 'African Americans', 'African Americans: highest doses from VKORC1 G allele and CYP2C9*1 frequency.'),
('e7dd906a-d94e-5cea-bffa-a973a9508925'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'Prasugrel active metabolite formed by:', '["CYP2C19 resulting in decreased functional activity","CES1 followed by CYP3A4/2B6","CYP2D6 mediated by specific receptor activation","CYP1A2 without affecting the primary tissue pathway","UGT1A1 leading to subsequent cellular adaptation"]'::jsonb, 'CES1 followed by CYP3A4/2B6', 'CES1 hydroxylation then CYP3A4/2B6 oxidation to active thiol metabolite.'),
('13bf9074-5ee2-5bb6-afbc-b89caadaa9f7'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'Prasugrel contraindicated in:', '["Hypertension","History of stroke/TIA","Diabetes","Hyperlipidemia","CKD"]'::jsonb, 'History of stroke/TIA', 'Contraindicated with prior stroke/TIA (increased ICH risk).'),
('92ae96d7-1c96-5ecc-8ed8-b00543b8b32f'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'Prasugrel faster onset than clopidogrel because:', '["Faster absorption resulting in decreased functional activity","More efficient CES1-mediated activation vs two-step CYP2C19","Longer t1/2 mediated by specific receptor activation","Greater binding without affecting the primary tissue pathway","Different mechanism leading to subsequent cellular adaptation"]'::jsonb, 'More efficient CES1-mediated activation vs two-step CYP2C19', 'CES1 single-step more efficient than CYP2C19 two-step activation.'),
('0065f2b2-1e05-5fec-bb19-2bcc1a86154f'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'Prasugrel greatest benefit in:', '["Elderly >75","Weight <60kg","ACS undergoing PCI","Stable angina","On OACs"]'::jsonb, 'ACS undergoing PCI', 'TRITON-TIMI 38: benefit in ACS patients undergoing PCI.'),
('bab40616-f609-5bd6-b055-f9dfd622a8ac'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'Prasugrel loading dose:', '["75 mg","300 mg","60 mg","10 mg","90 mg"]'::jsonb, '60 mg', '60 mg loading; maintenance 10 mg daily (5mg if <60kg).'),
('9760bc23-9eac-5e3f-96e4-a36d0954c03d'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'Prasugrel maintenance dose:', '["75 mg","10 mg (5mg if <60kg)","60 mg","90 mg BD","300 mg"]'::jsonb, '10 mg (5mg if <60kg)', '10 mg daily; 5mg if body weight <60kg.'),
('afe2638c-cb21-5375-aa73-0035eb453c80'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'Prasugrel more potent than clopidogrel because:', '["Inhibits COX-1 resulting in decreased functional activity","More efficient rapid activation, greater P2Y12 inhibition","Blocks GPIIb/IIIa mediated by specific receptor activation","Reversible without affecting the primary tissue pathway","Longer t1/2 leading to subsequent cellular adaptation"]'::jsonb, 'More efficient rapid activation, greater P2Y12 inhibition', 'CES1/CYP3A4/2B6 activation more efficient than CYP2C19-dependent.'),
('4b9da990-d942-56e9-a3bc-593752048dc8'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'Prasugrel not recommended for >75 years or prior stroke/TIA because:', '["Less effective resulting in decreased functional activity","Increased bleeding without ischemic benefit","Causes MI mediated by specific receptor activation","Not metabolized without affecting the primary tissue pathway","Expensive leading to subsequent cellular adaptation"]'::jsonb, 'Increased bleeding without ischemic benefit', 'Increased bleeding in these subgroups without offsetting benefit.'),
('67ce1287-93ba-522e-8aa7-3808cc1e0dd2'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'Pre-analytical variables in coagulation testing include:', '["Lab equipment malfunction resulting in decreased functional activity","Incorrect blood collection (wrong tube, difficult draw, partial fill)","Technician error mediated by specific receptor activation","Reagent deterioration without affecting the primary tissue pathway","Software errors leading to subsequent cellular adaptation"]'::jsonb, 'Incorrect blood collection (wrong tube, difficult draw, partial fill)', 'Incorrect tube, difficult venipuncture, partial fill, delayed transport, hemolysis.'),
('0dba0038-7470-5cff-8788-fd4100611550'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'Preferred anticoagulant in antiphospholipid syndrome:', '["DOACs","Warfarin","LMWH","UFH","Aspirin"]'::jsonb, 'Warfarin', 'Warfarin (target 2.5-3.5) remains standard; DOACs shown inferior in TRAPS trial.'),
('7c253ebc-300a-5c91-8581-60d46742b63e'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'Preferred anticoagulant in pregnancy:', '["Warfarin","DOACs","UFH or LMWH","Aspirin","Dipyridamole"]'::jsonb, 'UFH or LMWH', 'UFH/LMWH do not cross placenta, not teratogenic.'),
('9ef32c5b-0e37-54b0-b677-f830b7cf2b13'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'Preferred thrombolytic for STEMI single bolus:', '["Alteplase","Streptokinase","Tenecteplase","Reteplase","Urokinase"]'::jsonb, 'Tenecteplase', 'Single IV bolus convenience, comparable/superior efficacy.'),
('b814d89f-402f-5239-8087-12ae6dc83c1a'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'Primary DIC treatment:', '["Anticoagulants resulting in decreased functional activity","Treat underlying cause + supportive blood products","Thrombolytics mediated by specific receptor activation","Antiplatelets without affecting the primary tissue pathway","Vitamin K alone leading to subsequent cellular adaptation"]'::jsonb, 'Treat underlying cause + supportive blood products', 'Cornerstone: treat underlying cause; supportive: FFP, platelets, cryoprecipitate.'),
('6adba53e-3106-5281-9275-cdb19dd6c81e'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'Principal HIT clinical concern:', '["Bleeding resulting in decreased functional activity","Thrombosis (venous and arterial)","Infection mediated by specific receptor activation","Hypotension without affecting the primary tissue pathway","Renal failure leading to subsequent cellular adaptation"]'::jsonb, 'Thrombosis (venous and arterial)', 'Prothrombotic despite low platelets; thrombosis 30-50% untreated.'),
('e8535c93-68a7-54ac-9ad6-29129dbbcdf0'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'Protamine anaphylactoid reaction incidence approximately:', '["0.01%","0.2-3%","10%","50%","100%"]'::jsonb, '0.2-3%', '0.2-3%; higher risk with previous protamine exposure (fish allergy, prior insulin).'),
('4490d5f9-9a00-559f-a467-aad393b2eb46'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'Protamine dose for heparin reversal approximately:', '["1 mg per 100 units heparin","1 mg per 1000 units","10 mg per 100 units","100 mg per 100 units","1 mg per 1 unit"]'::jsonb, '1 mg per 100 units heparin', '1 mg per 100 units UFH given in previous 2-3 hours (max 50mg).'),
('8bb6e333-b808-543f-8e8b-f709ffb451fd'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'Protamine given by:', '["Oral resulting in decreased functional activity","Slow IV over 10 minutes","IM mediated by specific receptor activation","SC without affecting the primary tissue pathway","Rectal leading to subsequent cellular adaptation"]'::jsonb, 'Slow IV over 10 minutes', 'Slow IV push over 10 minutes to avoid hypotension/collapse.'),
('77a49994-c66e-5dcc-9032-9168606cee59'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'Protamine incomplete with LMWH because:', '["Does not bind","Fewer long chains for binding","Destroyed by protamine","Increases metabolism","No charge"]'::jsonb, 'Fewer long chains for binding', 'Shorter chains = fewer pentasaccharide sequences = 60% neutralization.'),
('8eb8d903-24f0-5f82-8647-e45303918e5c'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'Protamine less effective LMWH because shorter chains:', '["Completely bound resulting in decreased functional activity","Fewer pentasaccharide sequences for binding","Not affected mediated by specific receptor activation","Increase metabolism without affecting the primary tissue pathway","Too small to measure leading to subsequent cellular adaptation"]'::jsonb, 'Fewer pentasaccharide sequences for binding', 'Shorter chains = fewer high-affinity sequences for protamine binding.'),
('000ffb93-8e1b-57db-b541-ab90dea3a5c4'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'Protamine partially neutralizes LMWH because:', '["Does not bind resulting in decreased functional activity","Fewer long chains for protamine binding","Destroyed by protamine mediated by specific receptor activation","Increases metabolism without affecting the primary tissue pathway","No charge leading to subsequent cellular adaptation"]'::jsonb, 'Fewer long chains for protamine binding', 'LMWH shorter chains have fewer pentasaccharide sequences for protamine binding.'),
('4cf61353-d036-55e8-858c-a09458a7e72b'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'Protamine rapid IV causes hypotension because:', '["Vasodilator resulting in decreased functional activity","Direct cardiovascular depressant effect","Blocks platelets mediated by specific receptor activation","Inhibits thrombin without affecting the primary tissue pathway","Activates complement leading to subsequent cellular adaptation"]'::jsonb, 'Direct cardiovascular depressant effect', 'Rapid IV: severe hypotension, bradycardia, anaphylactoid reactions; give slowly over 10 min.'),
('4d8d240d-fe96-5685-9374-cb5099752d34'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'Protamine sulfate derived from:', '["Fish sperm (salmon)","Synthetic only","Bacteria","Human plasma","Plant extracts"]'::jsonb, 'Fish sperm (salmon)', 'Positively charged protein from salmon sperm.'),
('8efda016-361b-5d6a-8747-409114a3583e'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'Protamine sulfate reverses:', '["Warfarin","Heparin","Aspirin","Clopidogrel","Rivaroxaban"]'::jsonb, 'Heparin', 'Protamine binds heparin electrostatically, neutralizing anticoagulant effect.'),
('a220f539-86c1-581b-92b5-b57280712785'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'Protamine-heparin binding is:', '["Covalent bonding","Ionic/electrostatic interaction","Hydrogen bonding","Van der Waals forces","Hydrophobic interaction"]'::jsonb, 'Ionic/electrostatic interaction', 'Positive protamine charges bind negative heparin charges electrostatically.'),
('b01e999d-72b5-53e8-bf05-afe4bc90464a'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'Protein C causes thrombosis because:', '["Activates thrombin resulting in decreased functional activity","Normally inactivates Va and VIIIa (anticoagulant)","Inhibits fibrinolysis mediated by specific receptor activation","Activates platelets without affecting the primary tissue pathway","Inhibits vitamin K leading to subsequent cellular adaptation"]'::jsonb, 'Normally inactivates Va and VIIIa (anticoagulant)', 'APC inactivates Va and VIIIa; deficiency = thrombosis.'),
('593fec4b-cd9c-52e9-a196-56ebf136c54a'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'Protein C deficiency causes warfarin necrosis because:', '["Long half-life resulting in decreased functional activity","Protein C (short t1/2 6h) depleted before procoagulant factors","Activates protein C mediated by specific receptor activation","Causes thrombosis without affecting the primary tissue pathway","Inhibits warfarin leading to subsequent cellular adaptation"]'::jsonb, 'Protein C (short t1/2 6h) depleted before procoagulant factors', 'Rapid protein C depletion creates prothrombotic state initially.'),
('1b51c76e-35a2-51fc-91cd-858c03f7ba2f'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'Protein S functions as cofactor for:', '["Activated protein C","Protein Z","Protein S itself","Protein K","Protein X"]'::jsonb, 'Activated protein C', 'Protein S is cofactor for APC, enhancing inactivation of Va and VIIIa.'),
('0e31a136-7d56-5d9f-8afc-e1cc9ae87858'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'Recombinant factor VIII preferred because:', '["Cheaper resulting in decreased functional activity","Eliminates blood-borne viral infection risk","Longer t1/2 mediated by specific receptor activation","Fewer side effects without affecting the primary tissue pathway","Oral route leading to subsequent cellular adaptation"]'::jsonb, 'Eliminates blood-borne viral infection risk', 'Eliminates HIV, hepatitis B/C transmission risk.'),
('e44d568b-5029-5752-b7e1-013843cdb07c'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'Recombinant factor VIIa works in hemophilia with inhibitors by:', '["Replaces VIII resulting in decreased functional activity","Bypasses VIII/IX by directly activating factor X on platelet surface","Inhibits fibrinolysis mediated by specific receptor activation","Stimulates platelets without affecting the primary tissue pathway","Binds inhibitors leading to subsequent cellular adaptation"]'::jsonb, 'Bypasses VIII/IX by directly activating factor X on platelet surface', 'rFVIIa activates X directly on phospholipid surface, bypassing tenase complex.'),
('84e896c3-958d-58e3-8bf3-d0914ed4a775'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'Reperfusion arrhythmia (AIVR) after thrombolysis:', '["Stop thrombolytic","Sign of successful reperfusion","Sign of failed reperfusion","Contraindication","Needs cardioversion"]'::jsonb, 'Sign of successful reperfusion', 'AIVR indicates vessel reopening; benign, self-limiting.'),
('c948152f-d38f-5efa-995b-22e5f5fdbbbf'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'Residual platelet reactivity (RPR) on antiplatelet therapy refers:', '["Complete inhibition resulting in decreased functional activity","Persistent aggregation despite therapy (predicts thrombotic risk)","No function mediated by specific receptor activation","Increased production without affecting the primary tissue pathway","Destruction leading to subsequent cellular adaptation"]'::jsonb, 'Persistent aggregation despite therapy (predicts thrombotic risk)', 'Measurable activation despite therapy; associated with thrombotic events.'),
('f0c13119-d354-5ef4-a4aa-13988cb0c406'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'Reteplase double bolus possible because:', '["Shorter t1/2 resulting in decreased functional activity","Longer t1/2 (15-18min) allowing 10+10 units 30min apart","No fibrin binding mediated by specific receptor activation","Oral without affecting the primary tissue pathway","Antigenic leading to subsequent cellular adaptation"]'::jsonb, 'Longer t1/2 (15-18min) allowing 10+10 units 30min apart', 'Longer t1/2 enables convenient double bolus IV administration.'),
('2cf728bc-9a33-5322-9b2d-c922af45bcc1'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'Rifampin decreases warfarin because:', '["CYP2C9 inhibitor resulting in decreased functional activity","Potent CYP inducer (2C9, 3A4), increasing metabolism","Blocks absorption mediated by specific receptor activation","Inhibits VKORC1 without affecting the primary tissue pathway","Enhances vitamin K leading to subsequent cellular adaptation"]'::jsonb, 'Potent CYP inducer (2C9, 3A4), increasing metabolism', 'Induces CYP2C9/3A4, dramatically increasing warfarin metabolism.'),
('3402078a-6ba8-54f4-ada2-f5530d67cc72'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'Rivaroxaban is a:', '["Vitamin K antagonist","Direct factor Xa inhibitor","Direct thrombin inhibitor","Heparin analogue","Antiplatelet"]'::jsonb, 'Direct factor Xa inhibitor', 'Selectively and directly inhibits factor Xa (free and clot-bound).'),
('22fefb7f-00eb-5027-90a1-89c13806146f'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'Rivaroxaban reduced from 20mg to 15mg when CrCl:', '["<90","15-50 mL/min","<15",">100","No reduction"]'::jsonb, '15-50 mL/min', 'CrCl 15-50: 15mg OD with food.'),
('622c0d0e-789e-557e-baf7-29fa81cc8b0a'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'Rivaroxaban taken with food because:', '["Improves stability","Increases bioavailability (20mg dose)","Prevents GI effects","Prodrug","Enhances excretion"]'::jsonb, 'Increases bioavailability (20mg dose)', 'Bioavailability 20mg: 66% fasted to 100% with food.'),
('d7eeca7b-6fca-573a-9b68-f2ee59885f0d'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'Romiplostim/eltrombopag stimulate:', '["RBCs","WBCs","Platelets","All blood lines","Lymphocytes only"]'::jsonb, 'Platelets', 'Thrombopoietin receptor agonists for ITP; stimulate megakaryocytes.'),
('37b57291-3cbb-5ea8-9403-6e2061d93085'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'S-warfarin half-life approximately:', '["6 hours","24-48 hours","72-96 hours","1 week","1 month"]'::jsonb, '24-48 hours', 'S-warfarin 24-48h; R-warfarin 30-60h; overall 40h.'),
('67d4279b-d2f2-5f6b-8d33-a68c4ad26b13'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'S-warfarin more potent than R-warfarin by:', '["2-fold","3-5 fold","10-fold","Equal","R more potent"]'::jsonb, '3-5 fold', '3-5x more potent as VKORC1 inhibitor; metabolized by CYP2C9.'),
('dfe5f26f-a416-5fe8-8065-e9f9de654553'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'Schilling test assesses:', '["Iron absorption","Vitamin B12 absorption","Folate absorption","Calcium absorption","Zinc absorption"]'::jsonb, 'Vitamin B12 absorption', 'Evaluates B12 absorption and differentiates causes of malabsorption.'),
('6f4a3e36-b49d-57f7-8feb-4dc35adc895f'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'Secondary aspirin resistance most commonly caused by:', '["Genetic polymorphisms","Non-compliance/poor adherence","Hepatic disease","Renal failure","Thyroid disease"]'::jsonb, 'Non-compliance/poor adherence', 'Non-adherence most common; also drug interactions (ibuprofen blocking aspirin access to COX-1).'),
