('44357703-5064-58ae-99de-ef87f74eef84'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'Stent thrombosis risk highest in:', '["First 24h only resulting in decreased functional activity","First 30 days (especially first week)","After 6 months mediated by specific receptor activation","After 1 year without affecting the primary tissue pathway","Equal throughout leading to subsequent cellular adaptation"]'::jsonb, 'First 30 days (especially first week)', 'Highest when endothelialization incomplete; DAPT critical during this period.'),
('af3b333b-20e3-5121-a53b-ce7532af91b7'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'Streptokinase differs from alteplase:', '["Fibrin-specific resulting in decreased functional activity","Non-fibrin-specific bacterial protein, allergic reactions","No antigenicity mediated by specific receptor activation","More expensive without affecting the primary tissue pathway","Given as bolus leading to subsequent cellular adaptation"]'::jsonb, 'Non-fibrin-specific bacterial protein, allergic reactions', 'From streptococci; non-fibrin-specific, antigenic, can cause anaphylaxis.'),
('c370643c-b04f-5615-81fe-db5f6f0ec43a'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'Stroke risk in AF quantified by:', '["HAS-BLED","Wells score","CHADS2 or CHA2DS2-VASc","Geneva score","TIMI score"]'::jsonb, 'CHADS2 or CHA2DS2-VASc', 'CHADS2/CHA2DS2-VASc guide anticoagulation decisions in AF.'),
('e43d2110-1e85-5129-b977-39fee632339f'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'Subacute combined degeneration caused by deficiency of:', '["Iron","Vitamin B12","Vitamin C","Vitamin D","Folic acid"]'::jsonb, 'Vitamin B12', 'B12 deficiency causes demyelination of dorsal columns, corticospinal, spinocerebellar tracts.'),
('a06972d1-d84a-57c4-b555-9caff52bac0a'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'Supratherapeutic LMWH anti-Xa managed by:', '["Give protamine immediately resulting in decreased functional activity","Withhold next dose, recheck anti-Xa level","Start warfarin mediated by specific receptor activation","Give vitamin K without affecting the primary tissue pathway","Dialysis leading to subsequent cellular adaptation"]'::jsonb, 'Withhold next dose, recheck anti-Xa level', 'Withhold next dose, allow levels to fall, recheck.'),
('90f5a88f-50f3-5684-a9eb-d16f98763660'::uuid, 'Pharmacology (Paper 2)', 'Hematologic Coagulation - Hematologic Drugs', 'TDM important for warfarin but not DOACs because:', '["DOACs have no effect resulting in decreased functional activity","DOACs have predictable PK making routine monitoring unnecessary","Warfarin has no effect mediated by specific receptor activation","DOACs IV only without affecting the primary tissue pathway","Warfarin safer leading to subsequent cellular adaptation"]'::jsonb, 'DOACs have predictable PK making routine monitoring unnecessary', 'Predictable dose-response makes TDM unnecessary for DOACs.'),
