('2177103e-8824-552b-a0a6-10d7d24bf59b'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'CCHF geographic distribution:', '["Worldwide resulting in decreased functional activity","Africa, Middle East, Asia, Eastern Europe","Only Africa mediated by specific receptor activation","Only Asia without affecting the primary tissue pathway","Only Europe leading to subsequent cellular adaptation"]'::jsonb, 'Africa, Middle East, Asia, Eastern Europe', 'CCHF is endemic in Africa, Middle East, Asia, and Eastern Europe.'),
('3d5b84e9-bb48-5a6a-baa4-4f545756c65e'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'CCHF nosocomial transmission:', '["Never occurs","High risk without infection control","Only with needlestick","Only with contact","Only with respiratory"]'::jsonb, 'High risk without infection control', 'CCHF has high nosocomial transmission risk without proper infection control.'),
('8c6430e7-b1bd-5659-bd3d-6f08332ff451'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'In the study of Virology Pt2, HDV is transmitted via:', '["Respiratory droplets","Fecal-oral route","Percutaneous and sexual exposure","Vector-borne","Foodborne"]'::jsonb, 'Percutaneous and sexual exposure', 'HDV is transmitted via blood and sexual contact.'),
('578c2556-5b8a-5a18-a026-7f08d1ee2555'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'A 55-year-old male with diagnosed HIV infection presents with progressive dyspnea, fever, and a nonproductive cough. CD4 count is 120 cells/mcL. Chest X-ray reveals bilateral interstitial infiltrates. Silver stain of bronchoalveolar lavage fluid shows cup-shaped cysts. What is the most likely pathogen?', '["Streptococcus pneumoniae","Cytomegalovirus","Cryptococcus neoformans","Pneumocystis jirovecii","Mycobacterium tuberculosis"]'::jsonb, 'Pneumocystis jirovecii', 'Pneumocystis pneumonia (PCP) is a classic opportunistic infection in HIV patients with CD4 counts < 200 cells/mcL. Silver staining showing cup-shaped cysts in lavage fluid is diagnostic for Pneumocystis jirovecii.'),
('a27a2e56-1a7b-52d2-a4e5-01c620621a97'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'A 60-year-old male with diagnosed HIV infection presents with progressive dyspnea, fever, and a nonproductive cough. CD4 count is 120 cells/mcL. Chest X-ray reveals bilateral interstitial infiltrates. Silver stain of bronchoalveolar lavage fluid shows cup-shaped cysts. What is the most likely pathogen?', '["Pneumocystis jirovecii","Streptococcus pneumoniae","Cryptococcus neoformans","Cytomegalovirus","Mycobacterium tuberculosis"]'::jsonb, 'Pneumocystis jirovecii', 'Pneumocystis pneumonia (PCP) is a classic opportunistic infection in HIV patients with CD4 counts < 200 cells/mcL. Silver staining showing cup-shaped cysts in lavage fluid is diagnostic for Pneumocystis jirovecii.'),
('34c6cac3-335f-59a7-9d52-33ccd24cb06b'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'During therapeutic management of Virology Pt2, HCV screening in pregnancy:', '["Not recommended","Recommended for all","Only high-risk","Only first trimester","Only third trimester"]'::jsonb, 'Recommended for all', 'CDC recommends HCV screening for all pregnant women.'),
('190066f3-87ed-5703-a037-f71dd493d049'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'A 19-year-old student presents with fever, sore throat, and severe fatigue. Physical exam shows posterior cervical lymphadenopathy and splenomegaly. A peripheral blood smear shows atypical lymphocytes (reactive CD8+ T cells). The Monospot test is positive. What is the causative virus?', '["Adenovirus","Cytomegalovirus (CMV)","Epstein-Barr virus (EBV)","Human herpesvirus 6 (HHV-6)","Toxoplasma gondii"]'::jsonb, 'Epstein-Barr virus (EBV)', 'Infectious mononucleosis in young adults is most commonly caused by Epstein-Barr virus (EBV). The triad of fever, pharyngitis, and lymphadenopathy, accompanied by atypical lymphocytosis and a positive heterophile antibody (Monospot) test, is classic.'),
('8c3dac42-4cea-59e1-9d21-a0b6525d2739'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'In the study of Virology Pt2, HIV CD4 count defining AIDS:', '["<500 cells/mm3","<350 cells/mm3","<200 cells/mm3","<100 cells/mm3","<50 cells/mm3"]'::jsonb, '<200 cells/mm3', 'AIDS is defined by CD4 <200 cells/mm3 or AIDS-defining illnesses.'),
('de3c03ce-7174-53e5-9f45-a11213723db8'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'From a pathophysiological standpoint regarding Virology Pt2: HIV and metabolic syndrome:', '["No association","Increased risk with ART","Only with PIs","Only with NRTIs","Only in obese"]'::jsonb, 'Increased risk with ART', 'ART is associated with increased metabolic syndrome risk.'),
('e2b70846-f4af-5a3d-9389-f930415d88aa'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'Concerning diagnostic evaluations in Virology Pt2: HHV-7 is associated with:', '["Genital herpes only","Mono only","Chickenpox only","Roseola (also HHV-6)","KS only"]'::jsonb, 'Roseola (also HHV-6)', 'HHV-7, like HHV-6, is associated with roseola.'),
('7431d60a-9cce-5e82-9e38-946cf5bad527'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'ACE2 receptor function:', '["Viral entry receptor for SARS-CoV-2","CD8 co-receptor","CCR5 co-receptor","CD4 co-receptor","CXCR4 co-receptor"]'::jsonb, 'Viral entry receptor for SARS-CoV-2', 'ACE2 is the entry receptor for SARS-CoV-2 into host cells.'),
('edf99f14-2fb9-5da6-8bea-4dff9dc7f44f'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'Regarding clinical cases in Virology Pt2: VZV reactivation (shingles) risk factors:', '["Age >50","Immunosuppression","Stress","All of the above","None"]'::jsonb, 'All of the above', 'Risk factors include age, immunosuppression, and stress.'),
('f93e551b-8502-5b72-8469-09d332ada583'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'COVID-19 incubation period:', '["1-3 days resulting in decreased functional activity","2-14 days (average 5-6 days)","1-2 weeks mediated by specific receptor activation","3-4 weeks without affecting the primary tissue pathway","1 month leading to subsequent cellular adaptation"]'::jsonb, '2-14 days (average 5-6 days)', 'COVID-19 incubation period averages 5-6 days (range 2-14).'),
('cdd603d2-d756-5c44-ba6b-ddcaf2ff0604'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'COVID-19 common symptoms:', '["Fever + cough + dyspnea","Only fever","Only cough","Only dyspnea","No symptoms"]'::jsonb, 'Fever + cough + dyspnea', 'Common: fever, dry cough, dyspnea, fatigue, loss of taste/smell.'),
