('f26ceebe-4731-5ea2-8f8f-e4ed77fd8880'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'During therapeutic management of Virology Pt2, HAV has an incubation period of:', '["1-2 weeks","2-4 weeks","4-6 weeks","6-8 weeks","8-12 weeks"]'::jsonb, '2-4 weeks', 'HAV incubation period is typically 2-4 weeks (average 28 days).'),
('f6169899-9a43-5d70-af46-947722fe1898'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'Dexamethasone in COVID-19:', '["Always indicated resulting in decreased functional activity","Beneficial in severe/critical COVID (requiring O2)","Contraindicated mediated by specific receptor activation","Only in mild cases without affecting the primary tissue pathway","Not effective leading to subsequent cellular adaptation"]'::jsonb, 'Beneficial in severe/critical COVID (requiring O2)', 'Dexamethasone reduces mortality in severe COVID requiring oxygen.'),
('1de3d890-0192-5a36-afec-67e289e9bb99'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'A 50-year-old female presents for evaluation of chronic fatigue. Lab studies reveal the presence of HBsAg and HBeAg in the serum, with negative anti-HBs. Anti-HBc IgG is positive. What is the clinical status of this patient?', '["Chronic hepatitis B with low infectivity","Chronic hepatitis B with active viral replication","Immunity due to vaccination","Recovery from past infection","Acute hepatitis B infection"]'::jsonb, 'Chronic hepatitis B with active viral replication', 'The persistence of HBsAg for > 6 months indicates chronic HBV. The presence of HBeAg indicates high viral replication and high infectivity. Recovery/immunity would be marked by positive anti-HBs antibodies.'),
('bad89822-b353-5d85-bac1-d91ea4de4a36'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'COVID-19 mRNA vaccines:', '["Pfizer, Moderna","AstraZeneca, J&J","Sinovac, Sinopharm","Novavax","All of the above"]'::jsonb, 'Pfizer, Moderna', 'Pfizer-BioNTech and Moderna are mRNA vaccines.'),
