('8e580897-bac2-506b-80b6-a02e9d8f0086'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'A 30-year-old female presents for evaluation of chronic fatigue. Lab studies reveal the presence of HBsAg and HBeAg in the serum, with negative anti-HBs. Anti-HBc IgG is positive. What is the clinical status of this patient?', '["Immunity due to vaccination","Recovery from past infection","Acute hepatitis B infection","Chronic hepatitis B with active viral replication","Chronic hepatitis B with low infectivity"]'::jsonb, 'Chronic hepatitis B with active viral replication', 'The persistence of HBsAg for > 6 months indicates chronic HBV. The presence of HBeAg indicates high viral replication and high infectivity. Recovery/immunity would be marked by positive anti-HBs antibodies.'),
