('7f3aab8c-9f1a-567f-971e-8b584fe658c4'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'A 35-year-old female with diagnosed HIV infection presents with progressive dyspnea, fever, and a nonproductive cough. CD4 count is 120 cells/mcL. Chest X-ray reveals bilateral interstitial infiltrates. Silver stain of bronchoalveolar lavage fluid shows cup-shaped cysts. What is the most likely pathogen?', '["Cryptococcus neoformans","Pneumocystis jirovecii","Streptococcus pneumoniae","Cytomegalovirus","Mycobacterium tuberculosis"]'::jsonb, 'Pneumocystis jirovecii', 'Pneumocystis pneumonia (PCP) is a classic opportunistic infection in HIV patients with CD4 counts < 200 cells/mcL. Silver staining showing cup-shaped cysts in lavage fluid is diagnostic for Pneumocystis jirovecii.'),
('0aa0cb49-369e-5695-a8f9-6edc2edc4595'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'COVID-19 vaccine booster recommendations:', '["Not needed resulting in decreased functional activity","Recommended, especially with waning immunity and new variants","Only for elderly mediated by specific receptor activation","Only for immunocompromised without affecting the primary tissue pathway","Only for healthcare workers leading to subsequent cellular adaptation"]'::jsonb, 'Recommended, especially with waning immunity and new variants', 'Boosters recommended due to waning immunity and variant emergence.'),
('85b02579-72ab-5ebf-80a5-8bc298557229'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'COVID-19 and immunocompromised:', '["No increased risk resulting in decreased functional activity","Higher risk of severe disease and prolonged viral shedding","Lower risk mediated by specific receptor activation","Same as general population without affecting the primary tissue pathway","Only elderly immunocompromised leading to subsequent cellular adaptation"]'::jsonb, 'Higher risk of severe disease and prolonged viral shedding', 'Immunocompromised at higher risk of severe disease and prolonged infection.'),
