('48240c38-7ef8-5a71-a3e8-bc5de2a8b789'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'During therapeutic management of Virology Pt2, HBV reactivation risk during chemotherapy:', '["No risk","High risk, requires antiviral prophylaxis","Only with interferon","Only in HBsAg positive","Only in anti-HBc positive"]'::jsonb, 'High risk, requires antiviral prophylaxis', 'HBV reactivation is common during immunosuppressive therapy.'),
('15b21657-afe0-54f2-9bcd-6898d6c5f1af'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'Regarding clinical cases in Virology Pt2: HDV superinfection chronicity:', '["Never chronic","70-90% become chronic","Always chronic","50% chronic","Only in children"]'::jsonb, '70-90% become chronic', 'HDV superinfection leads to chronic HDV in 70-90% of cases.'),
('296872c5-651e-5db9-803c-26c458645b9d'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'COVID-19 and diabetes:', '["No association resulting in decreased functional activity","Diabetes increases severity; COVID can worsen glycemic control","Protective mediated by specific receptor activation","Only type 1 diabetes without affecting the primary tissue pathway","Only type 2 diabetes leading to subsequent cellular adaptation"]'::jsonb, 'Diabetes increases severity; COVID can worsen glycemic control', 'Diabetes is a major risk factor; COVID-19 can precipitate diabetic emergencies.'),
('b1485a82-bbc6-5ae1-b9c1-5001767f68a1'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'Valacyclovir better bioavailability than acyclovir:', '["Prodrug with 55% vs 15-30% absorption","Broader spectrum","Less nephrotoxicity","Longer half-life","IV available"]'::jsonb, 'Prodrug with 55% vs 15-30% absorption', 'L-valyl ester prodrug.'),
('4f905d58-85e7-5b0c-a0b2-83dc20bfda4a'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'Foscarnet inhibits:', '["Viral DNA polymerase directly (no TK needed)","Viral thymidine kinase accompanied by associated clinical symptoms","Viral protease mediated by specific receptor activation","Integrase without affecting the primary tissue pathway","Reverse transcriptase leading to subsequent cellular adaptation"]'::jsonb, 'Viral DNA polymerase directly (no TK needed)', 'Pyrophosphate analog, no activation required.'),
