('b96d3c8b-1648-5775-ae14-14de9d8ec730'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'A 60-year-old female with diagnosed HIV infection presents with progressive dyspnea, fever, and a nonproductive cough. CD4 count is 120 cells/mcL. Chest X-ray reveals bilateral interstitial infiltrates. Silver stain of bronchoalveolar lavage fluid shows cup-shaped cysts. What is the most likely pathogen?', '["Streptococcus pneumoniae","Cytomegalovirus","Pneumocystis jirovecii","Cryptococcus neoformans","Mycobacterium tuberculosis"]'::jsonb, 'Pneumocystis jirovecii', 'Pneumocystis pneumonia (PCP) is a classic opportunistic infection in HIV patients with CD4 counts < 200 cells/mcL. Silver staining showing cup-shaped cysts in lavage fluid is diagnostic for Pneumocystis jirovecii.'),
('01522d9e-4c2d-548c-8f97-bcadc976de73'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'EBV heterophile-negative mono:', '["Does not exist","CMV, HHV-6, toxoplasmosis, HIV","Only CMV","Only HHV-6","No other causes"]'::jsonb, 'CMV, HHV-6, toxoplasmosis, HIV', 'Heterophile-negative mono: CMV, HHV-6, toxoplasmosis, acute HIV.'),
('a9ef6041-6602-5412-920a-fdfd12664429'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'EBV serology VCA IgM:', '["Indicates past infection","Indicates acute infection","Indicates chronic infection","Indicates immunity","Not detectable"]'::jsonb, 'Indicates acute infection', 'VCA IgM appears early and indicates acute/recent EBV infection.'),
('0879d159-3bd7-5534-98e6-48b6b55d0f87'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'Concerning diagnostic evaluations in Virology Pt2: HCV does NOT cause:', '["Chronic hepatitis","Cirrhosis","Hepatocellular carcinoma","Cryoglobulinemia","Pancreatitis"]'::jsonb, 'Pancreatitis', 'HCV does not cause pancreatitis; it affects the liver and immune system.'),
('8c46f970-ca87-54db-b54c-89baac0f26ea'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'During therapeutic management of Virology Pt2, HIV and Kaposi sarcoma:', '["No association","HHV-8 associated, common in AIDS","Only with CD4 >200","Only in women","Only with treatment"]'::jsonb, 'HHV-8 associated, common in AIDS', 'KS is caused by HHV-8 and is an AIDS-defining illness.'),
('65e87bb2-d8aa-51f5-86eb-91022a1f1ac8'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'EBV mono clinical features:', '["Fever + pharyngitis + lymphadenopathy + fatigue","Only fever accompanied by associated clinical symptoms","Only sore throat mediated by specific receptor activation","Only lymphadenopathy without affecting the primary tissue pathway","No symptoms leading to subsequent cellular adaptation"]'::jsonb, 'Fever + pharyngitis + lymphadenopathy + fatigue', 'Classic triad: fever, pharyngitis, lymphadenopathy + fatigue.'),
('9d4c623c-ce9b-5205-87e6-6c28637f656d'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'In the study of Virology Pt2, HEV ORF2 encodes:', '["Non-structural proteins","Capsid protein","Polymerase","Protease","Integrase"]'::jsonb, 'Capsid protein', 'ORF2 encodes the capsid protein.'),
('c2394e7e-662c-5a84-96d9-4219369004a8'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'From a pathophysiological standpoint regarding Virology Pt2: HSV encephalitis typically affects:', '["Cerebellum","Brainstem","Temporal lobe","Occipital lobe","Spinal cord"]'::jsonb, 'Temporal lobe', 'HSV encephalitis typically affects the temporal lobe.'),
('f807711a-426d-57ca-a672-5f484d6fd25d'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'EBV and hairy leukoplakia:', '["No association resulting in decreased functional activity","Oral hairy leukoplakia in immunocompromised","Only in HIV mediated by specific receptor activation","Only in transplant without affecting the primary tissue pathway","Only in children leading to subsequent cellular adaptation"]'::jsonb, 'Oral hairy leukoplakia in immunocompromised', 'Oral hairy leukoplakia is caused by EBV in immunocompromised patients.'),
('1606b2d0-96af-56c7-b598-c7aecafab7d9'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'EBV and CNS complications:', '["Never occurs","Encephalitis, meningitis, GBS","Only encephalitis","Only meningitis","Only GBS"]'::jsonb, 'Encephalitis, meningitis, GBS', 'EBV can cause encephalitis, meningitis, and GBS.'),
('debeab80-4b76-5390-80a3-1be2d3eab637'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'Regarding clinical cases in Virology Pt2: HCV diagnosis initial test:', '["HCV RNA PCR","Anti-HCV EIA","Liver biopsy","HCV genotype","ALT level"]'::jsonb, 'Anti-HCV EIA', 'Anti-HCV EIA is the initial screening test.'),
('516561f6-3f86-50fe-9ecf-6635d607f486'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'A 25-year-old male presents for evaluation of chronic fatigue. Lab studies reveal the presence of HBsAg and HBeAg in the serum, with negative anti-HBs. Anti-HBc IgG is positive. What is the clinical status of this patient?', '["Chronic hepatitis B with low infectivity","Chronic hepatitis B with active viral replication","Immunity due to vaccination","Recovery from past infection","Acute hepatitis B infection"]'::jsonb, 'Chronic hepatitis B with active viral replication', 'The persistence of HBsAg for > 6 months indicates chronic HBV. The presence of HBeAg indicates high viral replication and high infectivity. Recovery/immunity would be marked by positive anti-HBs antibodies.'),
('cac5b70e-5590-5c03-84b8-c65a872babb6'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'EBV mono treatment:', '["Acyclovir","Ganciclovir","Supportive care","Antibiotics","Antivirals"]'::jsonb, 'Supportive care', 'No specific antiviral treatment; management is supportive.'),
('3e1047e4-7e08-5130-ab7a-ffe14b93aef7'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'EBV and hemophagocytic lymphohistiocytosis:', '["No association","EBV can trigger HLH","Only in children","Only in adults","Only in immunocompromised"]'::jsonb, 'EBV can trigger HLH', 'EBV is a common trigger for HLH, especially in children/young adults.'),
('047480fc-d047-522b-8435-38b098d7f5e9'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'A 70-year-old female presents for evaluation of chronic fatigue. Lab studies reveal the presence of HBsAg and HBeAg in the serum, with negative anti-HBs. Anti-HBc IgG is positive. What is the clinical status of this patient?', '["Acute hepatitis B infection","Immunity due to vaccination","Recovery from past infection","Chronic hepatitis B with low infectivity","Chronic hepatitis B with active viral replication"]'::jsonb, 'Chronic hepatitis B with active viral replication', 'The persistence of HBsAg for > 6 months indicates chronic HBV. The presence of HBeAg indicates high viral replication and high infectivity. Recovery/immunity would be marked by positive anti-HBs antibodies.'),
('a078bea4-3bde-564c-9cd6-85df74631741'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'EBV and autoimmune diseases:', '["No association","Linked to MS, SLE, RA","Only MS","Only SLE","Only RA"]'::jsonb, 'Linked to MS, SLE, RA', 'EBV infection is associated with increased risk of autoimmune diseases.'),
('8cfc2060-5abf-5086-84f7-7f6a62f0803c'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'In the study of Virology Pt2, HIV abacavir hypersensitivity:', '["Common (10%)","HLA-B*5701 associated","Only in Africans","Mild","Never occurs"]'::jsonb, 'HLA-B*5701 associated', 'Abacavir hypersensitivity is associated with HLA-B*5701 allele.'),
('ebe8ab50-b542-595d-8c96-850228a4300a'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'A 60-year-old female presents for evaluation of chronic fatigue. Lab studies reveal the presence of HBsAg and HBeAg in the serum, with negative anti-HBs. Anti-HBc IgG is positive. What is the clinical status of this patient?', '["Acute hepatitis B infection","Immunity due to vaccination","Recovery from past infection","Chronic hepatitis B with active viral replication","Chronic hepatitis B with low infectivity"]'::jsonb, 'Chronic hepatitis B with active viral replication', 'The persistence of HBsAg for > 6 months indicates chronic HBV. The presence of HBeAg indicates high viral replication and high infectivity. Recovery/immunity would be marked by positive anti-HBs antibodies.'),
('60a06272-9152-547e-8ae9-587e1307b649'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'Rabies brain tissue diagnosis:', '["Always needed","Post-mortem gold standard","Not available","Only in animals","Not reliable"]'::jsonb, 'Post-mortem gold standard', 'DFA of brain tissue is the gold standard, performed post-mortem.'),
('064d7591-d7bd-549b-8784-88fcc3542fa7'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'During therapeutic management of Virology Pt2, HAV diagnosis is confirmed by:', '["HAV IgM antibodies","HAV IgG antibodies","HAV RNA PCR","Liver biopsy","HAV antigen"]'::jsonb, 'HAV IgM antibodies', 'HAV IgM antibodies indicate acute/current infection.'),
('f1f18d60-c5fc-5cfd-a2d9-b47fe5d5feb6'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'Regarding clinical cases in Virology Pt2: Chronic HBV treatment first-line:', '["Ribavirin","Interferon only","Acyclovir","Tenofovir or entecavir","No treatment available"]'::jsonb, 'Tenofovir or entecavir', 'Nucleos(t)ide analogues (tenofovir/entecavir) are first-line for chronic HBV.'),
('7a9dee86-44d5-57e8-aa5e-815b40578e05'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'In the study of Virology Pt2, HAV belongs to which family:', '["Flaviviridae","Picornaviridae","Retroviridae","Hepadnaviridae","Coronaviridae"]'::jsonb, 'Picornaviridae', 'HAV belongs to Picornaviridae family.'),
('26020a5d-a75f-5509-b3c0-48d2b5d883f9'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'Rabies EEG findings:', '["Normal","Periodic sharp waves","Flat line","Alpha rhythm","Delta waves only"]'::jsonb, 'Periodic sharp waves', 'EEG may show periodic sharp wave complexes.'),
('919cb4f9-5002-5e5a-8656-4bdba9dfe00a'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'Concerning diagnostic evaluations in Virology Pt2: HDV coinfection with HBV prognosis:', '["Worse than HBV alone","Better than HBV alone","Same as HBV alone","Always fatal","Always chronic"]'::jsonb, 'Worse than HBV alone', 'HDV coinfection worsens the prognosis compared to HBV alone.'),
('326c9b45-08b6-5d4c-b958-80b6312347dd'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'Rabies immunoglobulin route:', '["Oral resulting in decreased functional activity","Infiltration around wound + IM","IV only mediated by specific receptor activation","Subcutaneous without affecting the primary tissue pathway","Intrathecal leading to subsequent cellular adaptation"]'::jsonb, 'Infiltration around wound + IM', 'RIG: infiltrate around wound + remaining dose IM at distant site.'),
('dd0a06f8-4180-52ad-b316-1fd600adc3c8'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'Rabies vaccine intradermal regimen:', '["Not approved resulting in decreased functional activity","2-site intradermal on days 0, 3, 7, 28","Single dose mediated by specific receptor activation","10 doses without affecting the primary tissue pathway","Only in developed countries leading to subsequent cellular adaptation"]'::jsonb, '2-site intradermal on days 0, 3, 7, 28', 'WHO-approved intradermal regimen saves vaccine dose.'),
('bb0417a1-a15c-5e1a-ad40-d973f4183df6'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'Rabies in developed countries source:', '["Dogs resulting in decreased functional activity","Wild animals (bats, raccoons, skunks)","Cats mediated by specific receptor activation","Rodents without affecting the primary tissue pathway","Birds leading to subsequent cellular adaptation"]'::jsonb, 'Wild animals (bats, raccoons, skunks)', 'In developed countries, wild animals are primary rabies source.'),
('60226f0a-d6d5-54f2-98d8-218ec22d971c'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'Rabies in India:', '["No cases","Endemic, dogs main source","Only bats","Only wildlife","Only cats"]'::jsonb, 'Endemic, dogs main source', 'India is endemic for rabies with dogs as primary source.'),
('506cf4b7-10b3-53b1-a4d3-cdfb8f44d29a'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'Concerning diagnostic evaluations in Virology Pt2: HAV transmission is primarily:', '["Sexual","Vertical","Blood/products","Fecal-oral","Respiratory"]'::jsonb, 'Fecal-oral', 'HAV is transmitted via fecal-oral route, often through contaminated food/water.'),
