('8e9b006a-a907-52c6-b85c-97b68605d36b'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'Influenza PB1 protein:', '["Hemagglutinin resulting in decreased functional activity","Polymerase subunit (RNA synthesis)","Neuraminidase mediated by specific receptor activation","Protease without affecting the primary tissue pathway","Integrase leading to subsequent cellular adaptation"]'::jsonb, 'Polymerase subunit (RNA synthesis)', 'PB1 catalyzes RNA polymerization.'),
('a892d71f-eca4-56ee-acc7-f5df134d6b47'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'In the study of Virology Pt2, HAV jaundice onset after exposure:', '["1 week","2 weeks","3-4 weeks","6-8 weeks","3 months"]'::jsonb, '3-4 weeks', 'Jaundice typically appears 3-4 weeks after exposure.'),
('3a5fd57c-d482-5f1d-92ed-9c3f8350abd6'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'Dengue virus serotypes:', '["2 resulting in decreased functional activity","3 accompanied by associated clinical symptoms","4 (DENV-1 to DENV-4)","5 without affecting the primary tissue pathway","6 leading to subsequent cellular adaptation"]'::jsonb, '4 (DENV-1 to DENV-4)', 'Dengue has 4 serotypes with cross-reactive but not cross-protective immunity.'),
('79fe58f5-688d-5ece-afa7-fc5f41dec678'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'A 65-year-old male presents for evaluation of chronic fatigue. Lab studies reveal the presence of HBsAg and HBeAg in the serum, with negative anti-HBs. Anti-HBc IgG is positive. What is the clinical status of this patient?', '["Immunity due to vaccination","Acute hepatitis B infection","Chronic hepatitis B with low infectivity","Chronic hepatitis B with active viral replication","Recovery from past infection"]'::jsonb, 'Chronic hepatitis B with active viral replication', 'The persistence of HBsAg for > 6 months indicates chronic HBV. The presence of HBeAg indicates high viral replication and high infectivity. Recovery/immunity would be marked by positive anti-HBs antibodies.'),
('f7d61308-6d0d-5527-8d30-b2610599c7ce'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'Dengue fever with warning signs:', '["Outpatient resulting in decreased functional activity","Hospital observation, IV fluids","ICU only mediated by specific receptor activation","Antivirals without affecting the primary tissue pathway","No treatment leading to subsequent cellular adaptation"]'::jsonb, 'Hospital observation, IV fluids', 'Warning signs require hospitalization and close monitoring.'),
('7d403d86-f0e5-58c4-b23e-de1c1df8583c'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'Regarding clinical cases in Virology Pt2: Anti-HBe indicates:', '["Active replication","Seroconversion (lower replication)","Acute infection","Vaccination","No infection"]'::jsonb, 'Seroconversion (lower replication)', 'Anti-HBe seroconversion indicates decreased viral replication.'),
('f6c4c3ce-f9dc-5cdc-81cf-4e7711a3b72f'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'A 60-year-old male presents for evaluation of chronic fatigue. Lab studies reveal the presence of HBsAg and HBeAg in the serum, with negative anti-HBs. Anti-HBc IgG is positive. What is the clinical status of this patient?', '["Chronic hepatitis B with active viral replication","Acute hepatitis B infection","Recovery from past infection","Immunity due to vaccination","Chronic hepatitis B with low infectivity"]'::jsonb, 'Chronic hepatitis B with active viral replication', 'The persistence of HBsAg for > 6 months indicates chronic HBV. The presence of HBeAg indicates high viral replication and high infectivity. Recovery/immunity would be marked by positive anti-HBs antibodies.'),
('f520e9b9-66bd-51b1-8fce-8305dc3647a4'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'A 35-year-old male with diagnosed HIV infection presents with progressive dyspnea, fever, and a nonproductive cough. CD4 count is 120 cells/mcL. Chest X-ray reveals bilateral interstitial infiltrates. Silver stain of bronchoalveolar lavage fluid shows cup-shaped cysts. What is the most likely pathogen?', '["Cytomegalovirus","Cryptococcus neoformans","Streptococcus pneumoniae","Pneumocystis jirovecii","Mycobacterium tuberculosis"]'::jsonb, 'Pneumocystis jirovecii', 'Pneumocystis pneumonia (PCP) is a classic opportunistic infection in HIV patients with CD4 counts < 200 cells/mcL. Silver staining showing cup-shaped cysts in lavage fluid is diagnostic for Pneumocystis jirovecii.'),
('8d819533-844d-5034-aa11-3f7e1a370af6'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'Zika and sexual transmission prevention:', '["Not necessary","Condoms or abstinence recommended","Only for men","Only for women","Only during pregnancy"]'::jsonb, 'Condoms or abstinence recommended', 'Condoms or abstinence recommended during and after travel to endemic areas.'),
('71a6b29c-cf54-54d8-b07e-e5f23502fde9'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'During therapeutic management of Virology Pt2, HDV and cirrhosis:', '["No association","Accelerates cirrhosis development","Prevents cirrhosis","Only causes acute disease","Same rate as HBV alone"]'::jsonb, 'Accelerates cirrhosis development', 'HDV accelerates cirrhosis development compared to HBV alone.'),
('0c3f4d24-6969-5ce1-9fc2-4ca85001dac5'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'Chikungunya and chronic joint disease:', '["Never occurs","20-30% develop chronic arthritis","Always occurs","Only in elderly","Only in children"]'::jsonb, '20-30% develop chronic arthritis', '20-30% of chikungunya patients develop chronic joint disease.'),
('821c9849-6f33-5e47-83c5-7c274fb7dc1a'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'Chikungunya vs rheumatoid arthritis:', '["Identical resulting in decreased functional activity","Chikungunya: symmetric, small joints; RA: different pattern","No overlap mediated by specific receptor activation","Same treatment without affecting the primary tissue pathway","Same prognosis leading to subsequent cellular adaptation"]'::jsonb, 'Chikungunya: symmetric, small joints; RA: different pattern', 'Chikungunya arthritis is often symmetric, affecting small joints.'),
('13f653c7-2474-5b87-9060-e1e064d9289b'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'From a pathophysiological standpoint regarding Virology Pt2: HIV wasting syndrome:', '["Weight loss >10% + chronic diarrhea/fever","Weight gain accompanied by associated clinical symptoms","Only in treated patients mediated by specific receptor activation","Never occurs without affecting the primary tissue pathway","Only in children leading to subsequent cellular adaptation"]'::jsonb, 'Weight loss >10% + chronic diarrhea/fever', 'Wasting syndrome: >10% weight loss with chronic diarrhea or fever.'),
('7286488f-91fc-5475-a873-3a6b34ae06ae'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'Concerning diagnostic evaluations in Virology Pt2: HEV RNA detection:', '["Not available","RT-PCR","ELISA","Western blot","Culture"]'::jsonb, 'RT-PCR', 'HEV RNA is detected by RT-PCR, useful in early and chronic infection.'),
('99066f91-4635-5fb1-8ffb-ccaba003207a'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'CCHF and bone marrow:', '["Normal","Bone marrow suppression","Hypercellular","Leukemia","Lymphoma"]'::jsonb, 'Bone marrow suppression', 'CCHF can cause bone marrow suppression.'),
('fde1bcc8-8222-5a5c-80e9-4597949ff70d'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'CCHF and liver histology:', '["Normal resulting in decreased functional activity","Hepatocyte necrosis, Councilman bodies","Fibrosis mediated by specific receptor activation","Cirrhosis without affecting the primary tissue pathway","Steatosis leading to subsequent cellular adaptation"]'::jsonb, 'Hepatocyte necrosis, Councilman bodies', 'CCHF liver shows hepatocyte necrosis with Councilman bodies.'),
('d5382a92-1191-53eb-bcb6-1c0dcea55cde'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'CCHF IV ribavirin loading:', '["30 mg/kg resulting in decreased functional activity","40 mg/kg accompanied by associated clinical symptoms","30 mg/kg IV then 15 mg/kg Q6H","10 mg/kg without affecting the primary tissue pathway","50 mg/kg leading to subsequent cellular adaptation"]'::jsonb, '30 mg/kg IV then 15 mg/kg Q6H', 'IV ribavirin: 30 mg/kg loading then 15 mg/kg Q6H.'),
('17968679-7f3f-5ef8-bafe-7378bafac124'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'COVID-19 Paxlovid contraindications:', '["None","Drug interactions (CYP3A4 substrates)","Hepatic impairment","Renal impairment","All of the above"]'::jsonb, 'All of the above', 'Paxlovid: drug interactions, hepatic/renal impairment require caution.'),
('bbe570dd-40c1-5661-927b-9f9bcaa2bd97'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'Concerning diagnostic evaluations in Virology Pt2: HIV dementia (HAD):', '["Never occurs","Progressive dementia in advanced HIV","Only in children","Only with treatment","Mild and reversible"]'::jsonb, 'Progressive dementia in advanced HIV', 'HIV-associated dementia occurs in advanced HIV disease.'),
