('6a5a059f-c2b8-5acb-9596-78b171a1f28d'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'COVID-19 and anosmia:', '["Never occurs","Common, especially with early variants","Only with severe disease","Only in elderly","Only in children"]'::jsonb, 'Common, especially with early variants', 'Anosmia/ageusia was common with earlier variants; less with Omicron.'),
('8600a179-04a6-5aa0-b17e-8de8aa70fdd6'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'COVID-19 and cytokine storm:', '["Does not occur resulting in decreased functional activity","IL-6, TNF-alpha driven hyperinflammation","Only in mild cases mediated by specific receptor activation","Only in children without affecting the primary tissue pathway","Only in elderly leading to subsequent cellular adaptation"]'::jsonb, 'IL-6, TNF-alpha driven hyperinflammation', 'Cytokine storm contributes to severe COVID-19 ARDS.'),
('76bf92b6-b62b-5631-a705-450d81a29fef'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'COVID-19 tocilizumab:', '["Antiviral resulting in decreased functional activity","IL-6 receptor antagonist (anti-inflammatory)","Antibiotic mediated by specific receptor activation","Antifungal without affecting the primary tissue pathway","Antiparasitic leading to subsequent cellular adaptation"]'::jsonb, 'IL-6 receptor antagonist (anti-inflammatory)', 'Tocilizumab blocks IL-6 receptor, used in severe COVID-19.'),
('938ace7b-5ed2-55f3-bf6f-b3f8a32b7c44'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'COVID-19 baricitinib:', '["Antiviral resulting in decreased functional activity","JAK inhibitor (anti-inflammatory)","Antibiotic mediated by specific receptor activation","Antifungal without affecting the primary tissue pathway","Antiparasitic leading to subsequent cellular adaptation"]'::jsonb, 'JAK inhibitor (anti-inflammatory)', 'Baricitinib is a JAK inhibitor used in severe COVID-19.'),
('332d1cc9-a199-5d4f-a492-467bf2b1e0f3'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'COVID-19 recovery plasma:', '["Not available resulting in decreased functional activity","Convalescent plasma (antibodies)","Antiviral mediated by specific receptor activation","Antibiotic without affecting the primary tissue pathway","Not effective leading to subsequent cellular adaptation"]'::jsonb, 'Convalescent plasma (antibodies)', 'Convalescent plasma contains anti-SARS-CoV-2 antibodies.'),
('ee950b45-8128-530f-aec7-c7bba7ea960e'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'COVID-19 and children:', '["Same severity as adults","Generally milder, but MIS-C possible","Never infected","More severe than adults","Asymptomatic only"]'::jsonb, 'Generally milder, but MIS-C possible', 'Children usually milder, but risk of MIS-C exists.'),
('d5dc13d9-e32e-59ba-a3bc-501d776cb525'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'COVID-19 and neonates:', '["Cannot be infected","Can be infected, usually mild","Always severe","Always fatal","Only from breast milk"]'::jsonb, 'Can be infected, usually mild', 'Neonates can be infected; most have mild disease.'),
('be328607-d1cd-5226-ae08-f5af43622b6f'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'From a pathophysiological standpoint regarding Virology Pt2: HDV treatment:', '["Interferon alpha","Ribavirin","Acyclovir","No effective treatment","Tenofovir"]'::jsonb, 'Interferon alpha', 'Interferon alpha is the main treatment for chronic HDV.'),
('f678424c-ccfe-5ec8-b6b6-4c8bea41186e'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'Concerning diagnostic evaluations in Virology Pt2: HBV precore mutant:', '["HBeAg positive, high replication","HBeAg negative, still replicates","HBsAg negative","No viral replication","Always acute infection"]'::jsonb, 'HBeAg negative, still replicates', 'Precore mutants do not produce HBeAg but still replicate.'),
('25af02b3-d453-5ff3-86f0-aa17960ee2e3'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'During therapeutic management of Virology Pt2, HBV vertical transmission prevention:', '["Maternal antivirals + neonatal HBIG + vaccine","Maternal vaccine only","Cesarean section only","No prevention needed","Breastfeeding avoidance"]'::jsonb, 'Maternal antivirals + neonatal HBIG + vaccine', 'Combined approach: maternal antivirals + neonatal HBIG + vaccine series.'),
('d4cc9760-99b7-5f6f-a2cd-c8adc7235d80'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'Regarding clinical cases in Virology Pt2: HDV coinfection with HBV prognosis:', '["Worse than HBV alone","Better than HBV alone","Same as HBV alone","Always fatal","Always chronic"]'::jsonb, 'Worse than HBV alone', 'HDV coinfection worsens the prognosis compared to HBV alone.'),
('b3c6f98d-64be-59aa-af77-6e6d120d3887'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'In the study of Virology Pt2, HCV occult infection:', '["HBsAg negative, HCV RNA detectable","Anti-HCV negative, HCV RNA detectable","Always symptomatic","Never causes disease","Only in immunocompromised"]'::jsonb, 'Anti-HCV negative, HCV RNA detectable', 'Occult HCV: anti-HCV negative but HCV RNA detectable in liver.'),
('c1dbc8ca-e892-5266-b514-2ca72b99e643'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'COVID-19 vaccine effectiveness waning:', '["Never wanes","Wanes over months, boosters help","Only wanes with inactivated","Only wanes with mRNA","Not measurable"]'::jsonb, 'Wanes over months, boosters help', 'Vaccine effectiveness wanes; boosters restore protection.'),
('68eaf691-882c-5b87-93a7-16f5a43b393b'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'Concerning diagnostic evaluations in Virology Pt2: HIV PEP timing:', '["Within 72 hours of exposure","Within 24 hours only","Within 1 week","Any time","Not effective"]'::jsonb, 'Within 72 hours of exposure', 'PEP must be started within 72 hours of exposure; earlier is better.'),
('1bf06f72-485d-598c-aa99-ed3174e08324'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'A 35-year-old male presents for evaluation of chronic fatigue. Lab studies reveal the presence of HBsAg and HBeAg in the serum, with negative anti-HBs. Anti-HBc IgG is positive. What is the clinical status of this patient?', '["Chronic hepatitis B with low infectivity","Recovery from past infection","Immunity due to vaccination","Acute hepatitis B infection","Chronic hepatitis B with active viral replication"]'::jsonb, 'Chronic hepatitis B with active viral replication', 'The persistence of HBsAg for > 6 months indicates chronic HBV. The presence of HBeAg indicates high viral replication and high infectivity. Recovery/immunity would be marked by positive anti-HBs antibodies.'),
('84132447-b0de-578b-9e4b-778a197087bc'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'COVID-19 and breastfeeding:', '["Contraindicated resulting in decreased functional activity","Safe, no significant transmission via breast milk","Only formula mediated by specific receptor activation","Only in developed countries without affecting the primary tissue pathway","Only with treatment leading to subsequent cellular adaptation"]'::jsonb, 'Safe, no significant transmission via breast milk', 'Breastfeeding is safe; SARS-CoV-2 not significantly transmitted via breast milk.'),
('27bf04c2-defb-5432-b690-94880daf0716'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'A 40-year-old male presents for evaluation of chronic fatigue. Lab studies reveal the presence of HBsAg and HBeAg in the serum, with negative anti-HBs. Anti-HBc IgG is positive. What is the clinical status of this patient?', '["Recovery from past infection","Chronic hepatitis B with low infectivity","Immunity due to vaccination","Chronic hepatitis B with active viral replication","Acute hepatitis B infection"]'::jsonb, 'Chronic hepatitis B with active viral replication', 'The persistence of HBsAg for > 6 months indicates chronic HBV. The presence of HBeAg indicates high viral replication and high infectivity. Recovery/immunity would be marked by positive anti-HBs antibodies.'),
('23b7622f-01c7-5163-906c-09f2431e98f9'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'EBV and gastric carcinoma:', '["No association resulting in decreased functional activity","10% of gastric carcinomas EBV-associated","All gastric cancers mediated by specific receptor activation","Only in Asia without affecting the primary tissue pathway","Only in elderly leading to subsequent cellular adaptation"]'::jsonb, '10% of gastric carcinomas EBV-associated', '10% of gastric carcinomas are EBV-associated.'),
('5f983615-88ca-5199-87fa-251742901d3c'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'Concerning diagnostic evaluations in Virology Pt2: HIV and breastfeeding:', '["Always contraindicated","Recommended in resource-limited settings with ART","Only formula feeding","Only in developed countries","No risk of transmission"]'::jsonb, 'Recommended in resource-limited settings with ART', 'In resource-limited settings, breastfeeding with ART is recommended.'),
('63989ade-3324-5b83-82c5-11ca3e693187'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'EBV LMP2A function:', '["Structural protein resulting in decreased functional activity","Mimics B-cell receptor signaling","Polymerase mediated by specific receptor activation","Protease without affecting the primary tissue pathway","Integrase leading to subsequent cellular adaptation"]'::jsonb, 'Mimics B-cell receptor signaling', 'LMP2A mimics BCR signaling, promoting B-cell survival.'),
('786262a9-bf45-5ec6-af98-4ccf1146d7d9'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'Regarding clinical cases in Virology Pt2: HBV test for screening blood donors:', '["HBV DNA only","HBsAg","Anti-HBc","HBeAg","Liver function tests"]'::jsonb, 'HBsAg', 'HBsAg is the primary screening test for blood donors.'),
('e0883ead-fca3-562f-a7c1-dd43cb7fc377'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'EBV and chronic fatigue syndrome:', '["No association resulting in decreased functional activity","EBV may trigger CFS/ME in some patients","Always causes CFS mediated by specific receptor activation","Only in elderly without affecting the primary tissue pathway","Only in children leading to subsequent cellular adaptation"]'::jsonb, 'EBV may trigger CFS/ME in some patients', 'EBV infection has been proposed as a trigger for CFS/ME.'),
('fc298dd1-2e5f-5900-be47-4a2815b504fe'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'From a pathophysiological standpoint regarding Virology Pt2: VZV (chickenpox) treated with:', '["Ribavirin","Ganciclovir","Acyclovir","Foscarnet","Cidofovir"]'::jsonb, 'Acyclovir', 'Acyclovir is first-line for VZV infections.'),
('a9f576e8-2694-5e03-b6f3-bebbccdc413f'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'EBV and lymphomatoid granulomatosis:', '["No association resulting in decreased functional activity","EBV-associated angiocentric lymphoproliferation","Only in children mediated by specific receptor activation","Only in elderly without affecting the primary tissue pathway","Only in immunocompetent leading to subsequent cellular adaptation"]'::jsonb, 'EBV-associated angiocentric lymphoproliferation', 'Lymphomatoid granulomatosis is EBV-driven angiocentric lymphoproliferation.'),
('9436d387-8a3e-5532-a82a-97ac64da1813'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'COVID-19 and mucormycosis treatment:', '["Antibiotics resulting in decreased functional activity","Amphotericin B + surgical debridement","Antivirals mediated by specific receptor activation","Antifungals only without affecting the primary tissue pathway","No treatment leading to subsequent cellular adaptation"]'::jsonb, 'Amphotericin B + surgical debridement', 'Mucormycosis requires amphotericin B + aggressive surgical debridement.'),
('5887096c-daab-502b-9bcf-c0b9d010989b'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'Regarding clinical cases in Virology Pt2: HBV treatment endpoint:', '["HBsAg loss (functional cure)","HBeAg seroconversion","HBV DNA undetectable","All of the above","None"]'::jsonb, 'All of the above', 'Treatment endpoints: HBV DNA suppression, HBeAg seroconversion, HBsAg loss.'),
('f0cdf404-9f6c-56b7-8b32-4df37303b78e'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'COVID-19 rebound after Paxlovid:', '["Never occurs resulting in decreased functional activity","Viral rebound possible after stopping treatment","Common mediated by specific receptor activation","Only in severe cases without affecting the primary tissue pathway","Only in elderly leading to subsequent cellular adaptation"]'::jsonb, 'Viral rebound possible after stopping treatment', 'Viral rebound can occur after completing Paxlovid course.'),
('a9d773e5-09c1-57d8-a38d-89d2f6ec8d03'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'COVID-19 and renal injury:', '["No renal involvement","Acute kidney injury in severe cases","Only in elderly","Only with pre-existing renal disease","Only with treatment"]'::jsonb, 'Acute kidney injury in severe cases', 'AKI occurs in severe COVID-19, multiorgan involvement.'),
('d8d98d25-3209-5007-8da2-96bd33d8b8f1'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'Concerning diagnostic evaluations in Virology Pt2: Ramsay Hunt syndrome:', '["HHV-6","HSV encephalitis","CMV retinitis","VZV geniculate ganglion","EBV mono"]'::jsonb, 'VZV geniculate ganglion', 'Ramsay Hunt is caused by VZV reactivation in geniculate ganglion.'),
('f1646c70-5e37-5b63-b15a-39e17f9fd33a'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'Mumps virus family:', '["Picornaviridae","Paramyxoviridae","Coronaviridae","Rhabdoviridae","Flaviviridae"]'::jsonb, 'Paramyxoviridae', 'Mumps virus belongs to Paramyxoviridae family, genus Rubulavirus.'),
('427341ca-b2a9-575a-9b0d-e39dfc1e0f3a'::uuid, 'General Pathology Microbiology Immunology (Paper 2)', 'Virology - Virology Part 2', 'Regarding clinical cases in Virology Pt2: HEV and organ transplantation:', '["No risk","High risk of chronic HEV","Only risk in liver transplant","Only risk in kidney transplant","Only risk in bone marrow transplant"]'::jsonb, 'High risk of chronic HEV', 'Solid organ transplant recipients are at high risk of chronic HEV.'),
